description:
A discovered `runtime/loop/index.mjs` target whose runtime env is missing `ANICCA_HOME` (`target.aniccaHome` is null/empty) is SILENTLY DROPPED from the registry-drift check entirely -- no entry, not even an `unobservable` FAIL, ever appears in `registryDrift` for that target. The code is:
```
if (target.aniccaHome && !seenHomes.has(target.aniccaHome)) {
  seenHomes.add(target.aniccaHome);
  const copyPath = path.join(target.aniccaHome, 'skills', 'registry.json');
  registryCopies.push({ copyPath, registryOrNull: await readRegistry(copyPath) });
}
```
When `target.aniccaHome` is falsy, this whole block is skipped -- nothing is pushed to `registryCopies` for that target, so it never surfaces anywhere in the report. This is a direct, verbatim violation of REQ-010's own edge case (behavioral-spec.md:387-389: 'ANICCA_HOME または XPC_SERVICE_NAME が実行時 env に存在しないプロセスが見つかった: REQ-004 に従い、そのプロセスについて `reason: "unobservable"` の FAIL を返す（黙って対象から除外しない）') and REQ-004's fail-closed principle in general -- a target whose registry-copy location cannot be determined is exactly the 'observation attempt failed' case REQ-004 exists to cover, yet it produces zero output instead of an explicit FAIL.
By contrast, the SAME missing-token scenario on the brain-drift side (missing `xpcServiceName`) IS handled correctly two lines above (`target.xpcServiceName ? await readPlistEnv(...) : null`, which flows into `detectBrainDrift`'s null-declaredConfig unobservable-FAIL path) -- the asymmetry shows this is a real gap, not an intentional design choice.
This is UNTESTED: config-drift.test.mjs:353-362 only verifies that the PURE parser `parseIndexLoopProcesses` correctly returns `aniccaHome: null` instead of dropping the record from ITS OWN return value -- no test anywhere (config-drift.test.mjs or config-drift-detector.test.mjs) drives `runConfigDriftDetector` with a fixture target that has `aniccaHome: null` and asserts an `unobservable` entry appears in `registryDrift`. The composed detector's own test suite (config-drift-detector.test.mjs) never constructs a ps-line fixture missing the `ANICCA_HOME=` token.
